# Master Plan: Premium Spices & Seasonal Fruits E-Commerce Platform
# ================================================================
# Phases are designed for maximum parallelization.
# Dependencies between phases are marked explicitly.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 0: Project Initialization
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Estimated: 1 session | Blocks: ALL other phases

- [ ] Initialize Next.js project (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS)
- [ ] Install core dependencies (zustand, stripe, @supabase/ssr, cloudinary)
- [ ] Configure environment variables (.env.local.example)
- [ ] Set up Tailwind theme (organic color palette, typography - Playfair Display + Inter)
- [ ] Create project folder structure (as defined in system-design.md)
- [ ] Configure next.config.ts (Cloudinary image domains, redirects)

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 1: Core Auth & Database Setup
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Estimated: 2 sessions | Blocks: Phase 2, 3, 4
# Can parallelize: [1A] and [1B] are independent

## [1A] Supabase Database Schema
- [ ] Write migration: 001_create_profiles.sql (profiles + addresses)
- [ ] Write migration: 002_create_categories.sql
- [ ] Write migration: 003_create_products.sql (products, variants, images)
- [ ] Write migration: 004_create_orders.sql (orders, order_items, cart_items)
- [ ] Write migration: 005_create_subscriptions.sql (plans, items, user_subscriptions)
- [ ] Write migration: 006_create_seasonal_rules.sql (rules + is_product_available function)
- [ ] Create storefront_products view
- [ ] Set up Row Level Security policies for all tables
- [ ] Write seed.sql with sample spices, fruits, and seasonal rules

## [1B] Auth & Middleware
- [ ] Configure Supabase Auth client (browser + server)
- [ ] Create auth callback route handler
- [ ] Build Next.js middleware for protected routes
- [ ] Create Zustand auth store
- [ ] Build Login page (/login)
- [ ] Build Register page (/register)
- [ ] Build basic Profile page (/profile)

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 2: Seasonal Logic Engine
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Estimated: 1-2 sessions | Depends on: Phase 1A
# Can parallelize: [2A] and [2B] are independent

## [2A] Backend Seasonal Logic
- [ ] Verify is_product_available() function handles edge cases
- [ ] Create Supabase Edge Function: daily catalog revalidation trigger
- [ ] Build API route for fetching seasonal products with filters
- [ ] Add client-side seasonal availability hook (use-seasonal.ts)

## [2B] Admin Seasonal Management
- [ ] Build admin page: manage seasonal rules per product
- [ ] Add seasonal rule CRUD (create, edit, delete rules)
- [ ] Preview: "Show products visible on [selected date]" tool
- [ ] Seasonal badge component (shows "In Season", "Coming Soon", "Last Days")

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 3: Spice Subscription Module
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Estimated: 2 sessions | Depends on: Phase 1A, Phase 1B
# Can parallelize: [3A] and [3B] after Stripe setup

## [3A] Stripe Subscription Backend
- [ ] Configure Stripe products and prices for subscription plans
- [ ] Build API route: create Stripe Checkout session (subscription mode)
- [ ] Build API route: Stripe webhook handler
  - [ ] Handle: checkout.session.completed
  - [ ] Handle: invoice.paid
  - [ ] Handle: customer.subscription.updated
  - [ ] Handle: customer.subscription.deleted
- [ ] Sync subscription status to user_subscriptions table

## [3B] Subscription Frontend
- [ ] Build subscription plans page (/subscriptions)
- [ ] Build "How It Works" section with step-by-step visual
- [ ] Build subscription management page (/account/subscriptions)
  - [ ] Display active subscription details
  - [ ] Pause / Resume functionality
  - [ ] Cancel at period end
- [ ] Build subscription success/confirmation page

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 4: High-Performance Frontend with SEO
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Estimated: 3-4 sessions | Depends on: Phase 1, 2
# Can parallelize: [4A], [4B], [4C], [4D] are largely independent

## [4A] Core Layout & Navigation
- [ ] Build root layout with Google Fonts (Playfair Display + Inter)
- [ ] Build Header component (logo, nav, cart icon with badge, auth)
- [ ] Build Footer component (links, newsletter, social)
- [ ] Build MobileNav component (bottom nav bar, hamburger menu)
- [ ] Build storefront layout (wraps header + footer)

## [4B] Product Pages
- [ ] Build ProductCard component (image, name, price, variant pills)
- [ ] Build ProductGrid component (responsive bento-style grid)
- [ ] Build Spice Catalog page (/spices) with filters and sorting
- [ ] Build Fruit Catalog page (/fruits) with seasonal indicators
- [ ] Build Product Detail page (image gallery, variant selector, add-to-cart)
- [ ] Build VariantSelector component (weight buttons: 50g, 100g, 500g)
- [ ] Build related products section

## [4C] Cart & Checkout
- [ ] Build Zustand cart store with persistence
- [ ] Build CartDrawer component (slide-out sidebar)
- [ ] Build Cart page (/cart) with item list, quantity controls
- [ ] Build checkout flow → Stripe Checkout redirect
- [ ] Build order confirmation page (/checkout/success)
- [ ] Build order history page (/account/orders)

## [4D] Homepage & SEO
- [ ] Build hero section (full-bleed seasonal imagery, CTA)
- [ ] Build "Featured Spices" section (curated product grid)
- [ ] Build "In Season Now" section (dynamic seasonal fruits)
- [ ] Build "Why Choose Us" section (trust badges, values)
- [ ] Build "Subscription CTA" section (monthly box promo)
- [ ] Implement generateMetadata() on every page
- [ ] Add JSON-LD structured data (Product, Offer, BreadcrumbList)
- [ ] Set up robots.ts and sitemap.ts
- [ ] Add Open Graph and Twitter Card meta tags

## [4E] Polish & Performance
- [ ] Configure Cloudinary image loader for Next.js
- [ ] Add blur placeholders for all product images
- [ ] Implement scroll-triggered animations (Intersection Observer)
- [ ] Add hover micro-animations on product cards
- [ ] Lighthouse audit and performance optimization
- [ ] Cross-browser and mobile responsiveness testing
